' Design pattern — Database per Service.
'
' Drawn with TWO services rather than all six: the rule is what matters, not the
' inventory, and six service/database pairs lay out ~3:1 and shrink to a strip.
' The note carries the full list instead.
'
' The point of the diagram is the two crossed dashed arrows. Nothing technically
' stops a service opening a connection to another service's database — the
' constraint is a design rule, and the diagram is where it gets stated.
'
' Two things kept deliberately OUT of this diagram, both learned by rendering it:
'   - The message bus and its event arrows. They belong to the pub/sub pattern,
'     and adding them here put six labelled edges through the middle of the
'     figure; the labels collided and nothing was readable.
'   - Free placement of the databases. Without the hidden edge below, smetana
'     ordered them classroomdb-then-users_db against the services above them,
'     so the two OWNERSHIP arrows crossed and read as the forbidden ones.
@startuml
!include _style.puml
skinparam linetype ortho

rectangle "خدمة إدارة المستخدمين" as UMS
rectangle "خدمة الفصول الدراسية" as CS

database "users_db" as UDB
database "classroomdb" as CDB

' Pin both rows left-to-right so each service sits directly above its own
' database and only the forbidden arrows cross. Do not remove.
UMS -[hidden]right- CS
UDB -[hidden]right- CDB

UMS --> UDB : تقرأ وتكتب
CS --> CDB : تقرأ وتكتب

UMS ..> CDB : ممنوع
CS ..> UDB : ممنوع

note bottom of UDB
  لكل خدمة قاعدتها وحدها: users_db، classroomdb،
  streaming_db، knowledgedb، liveassistantdb.
  وخدمة البريد بلا قاعدة أصلًا.
  ولا تصل خدمةٌ إلى قاعدة غيرها، بل تتبادل الخدمات
  عبر الناقل، أو بنداء HTTP داخلي حين يلزم جواب.
end note
@enduml
